// Pixel art as data: one character per pixel, '.' is clear, every other
// character is a palette key. Authored with a scratch generator, then
// committed as plain grids: edit the rows here directly.
//
// Chapter 4-3, the Seaport at sunrise: the timber harborwalk on a granite
// seawall, piers, containers, cranes, the cantilevered museum. Sunrise
// palette (warm gold lights, violet shadows), same art language. Tiles are
// 16 x 16, anchor top left, variants with fps 0 (the rooftop layout).
// roofTop is the harborwalk deck (row 0 its sunlit edge, boards, a bolted
// fascia) on the granite seawall (variant 1 a feather and salt stains,
// variant 2 a steel cleat); roofEdgeLeft and roofEdgeRight its ends;
// roofFill the seawall (variant 1 weed and barnacles on a joint, variant 2
// an iron mooring ring with a rust run); oneWay a pier on timber pilings;
// stone a rust red shipping container's corrugated side (stacks make
// walls; the top rail is lit); spikes broken concrete with rusted rebar
// (hazard); brick a slatted cargo crate (breakable); auraBlock the sigma
// crate in a blue container frame; vent a scupper through the seawall; pipe
// a steel water main run sideways (tileable).
//
// Decor anchor is the bottom left. museumOverhang (the goal: a glass box
// cantilevered far out over a timber grandstand, held by a solid core at
// the left with a lit doorway at (5, 41)): the glass takes the sunrise; 4
// frames of a glint sliding along it, loop. Stand the goal at its right
// edge, under the overhang.
//
// HOOK: 16 x 24, a crane's hook block, the hook, slings and a short
// spreader beam she stands on (an I beam with hazard stripes, its top on row
// 17, 16 px wide). anchor (8, 17) is the beam's top centre: draw it at the
// hook's platform point (w.hooks[i].px, py) and draw the cable from the
// pivot (x, y) to the block's top at (px, py - 17). Rotate nothing: the
// beam stays level as it swings.
//
// GUST: 16 x 8 wind streaks, 3 frames, fps 10, loop (thin, long, fading),
// anchor (8, 4), facing right (mirror for dir -1). Draw a few per gust zone
// on screen while it warns (sparse, frame 0) and blows (dense, all frames).
// The keys are translucent white.
//
// HARBOR_GLOW lists the keys that glow: 0 sun glint, 1 sun core, 2 red
// beacon, 3 lamp, 4 tower green, 5 deep gold, ^ ~ aura, 7 8 gold halos, *
// red halo.
//
// HARBOR_BACKDROP: three 512 px tileable strips, bottom row one colour so it
// can be lifted. far (96): the airport across the water at sunrise, long
// low terminals and hangars pale with distance, the control tower's thin
// shaft and flared green cab with its red light, parked tails, the
// approach lights dotted along the water's edge with a green threshold,
// then the water with gold glints. The sun disc is the sky preset's. mid
// (80): the container quay backlit by the low sun, gold rims on every top
// edge: a container ship alongside with stacked boxes and its bridge house,
// four ship to shore cranes (booms raised like arms, one level with a
// spreader hanging), red lights on the boom tips, a warehouse, harborwalk
// lamps fading. near (64): harbor water close by, swells lit gold on their
// crests, old pilings, a moored lobster boat with its wheelhouse forward.
